MOD({id:"m5a",d:"d5",title:"Supply Chain Orchestration",
lede:"How supply requests become POs, work orders, transfer orders or reservations, and how exceptions are managed.",
topics:["Describe the Supply Chain Orchestration flow","Analyze and manage business flows and exceptions within SCO"],
sections:[
{t:"What SCO does",h:"<ul>\n<li>Receives supply requests, launches predefined processes, automates change management and gives a 360° view of supply creation.</li>\n<li>Request sources: Planning Central, GOP + OM (back-to-back), Inventory min-max, PAR, spreadsheet upload, requisitions, Manage Item Quantities, supply request web service.</li>\n<li><b>Supply orchestration</b> gets goods into your warehouse (may or may not be for a sales order). <b>Order orchestration</b> gets goods to the customer (always a sales order).</li></ul>\n<p class=\"src\">Source: Advanced Fulfillment, lesson 2; OM course overview slides</p>"},
{t:"How a request is processed",h:"<ol>\n<li>Receive request (decompose). Interface data is processed by <b>Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface</b>.</li>\n<li>Prepare: map attributes, run execution rules, enrichment, assign and launch process.</li>\n<li>Execute the orchestration process: process planning, change management, tracking.</li>\n<li>Interact with execution systems (Procurement, Manufacturing, Inventory) via web services.</li></ol>\n<p>Entities: supply order, supply order line, tracking line, and transfer/buy/make order details capturing TO, PO and WO data.</p><div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: running the interface</b><ul>\n<li>Scheduled Processes → <b>Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface</b>. Key parameter: <b>Supply Request System</b>; only requests from that source are picked up.</li>\n<li>Values: Oracle Fusion Planning Central, Self Service Procurement, Order Management, Inventory Management, External, Common Work Execution, Supply Chain Orchestration, Replenishment Planning. Other parameters: organisation, request batch numbers and dates, batch size.</li>\n<li>Advanced → Schedule: As soon as possible or Using a schedule.</li></ul><small>Advanced Supply Chain & Fulfillment exercises</small></div>"},
{t:"Key setups",h:"<ul>\n<li>FSM: Manufacturing and SC Materials Mgmt → Supply Chain Orchestration → Define Supply Chain Orchestration Foundation.</li>\n<li><b>Supply execution document creation rules</b>: TO or PO? Default = TO. Keys: source + destination org (or item too).</li>\n<li><b>Supply order defaulting and enrichment rules</b>: TO direct to Inventory (default) or via OM; can also set e.g. WO status to released or shipment priority. Keys: item + org. B2B transfers can't go via OM.</li>\n<li>Optional: lookups, attachment categories, user-defined scheduler jobs, service mapper (e.g. pass SO EFFs downstream).</li>\n<li>Data security: Supply Chain Operations Manager sees everything; restrict via custom role and policy, then run Import User and Role Application Security Data.</li></ul>"},
{t:"Tracking and change management",h:"<ul>\n<li>Supply Lines Overview buckets: <b>Errors</b> (technical/functional failure), <b>Exceptions</b> (supply ≠ demand, change mgmt couldn't fix), <b>Jeopardy</b> (late vs need-by), <b>On-track</b>.</li>\n<li>Grouped by supply type (Make, Buy, Transfer, ATP), source, destination, item. Closed orders hidden by default.</li>\n<li>Drill: Overview → Manage Supply Lines (resubmit, mark inactive) → Supply Order Details → execution document.</li>\n<li>Changes: supply-side (qty, cancel, date, split) and demand-side (cancel, qty, need-by date). If supply can't adjust → exception to the fulfilment manager.</li>\n<li>Example: demand 100, PO cut to 75 → SCO seeks another source for 25; none found → exception.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"focus\"><b>Exam focus</b>Know the four buckets and the difference between an error and an exception.</div><div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: the SCO work area</b><ul>\n<li>Overview has two tiles: <b>Supply Requests</b> and <b>Supply Alerts</b>, filterable by request source, requested by, business flow and status.</li>\n<li>Supply request (header) → View Supply Request Line Details. Sections: <b>Supply Details</b> (receipt, reservation, PO, requisition), <b>Orchestration Plan</b> (e.g. Purchase Requisition → Purchase Order → Reservation → Put Away → Fulfillment Completion), <b>Service Mapping Details</b> (attributes carried downstream, e.g. PurchaseRequestLine NoteToSupplier / NoteToReceiver).</li>\n<li>Supply lines have tabs Orchestration Plan, Execution Documents, Buy, Make, Transfer, On Hand.</li></ul><small>Advanced Supply Chain & Fulfillment exercises</small></div>"}
]});
MOD({id:"m5b",d:"d5",title:"Back-to-back fulfilment",
lede:"Creating and reserving supply for a specific sales order, then shipping it from your warehouse.",
topics:["Configure the back-to-back process","Execute the back-to-back process"],
sections:[
{t:"What back-to-back is",h:"<ul>\n<li>Supply is created for a specific order, received in your warehouse, reserved to the order until shipping.</li>\n<li>For high-cost, non-stocked or slow-moving items, or when space near the customer is expensive.</li>\n<li>Fulfilment selection after scheduling: internal warehouse + item not B2B enabled → <b>standard</b>; scheduled to supplier → <b>drop ship</b>; internal warehouse + B2B enabled → <b>back-to-back</b>.</li>\n<li>Variants (GOP recommendation): <b>Buy</b> (PO), <b>Make</b> (WO), <b>Transfer</b> (TO), <b>On hand</b> (reservation).</li></ul>\n<p class=\"src\">Source: Advanced Fulfillment, lessons 5–7; OM course B2B slides</p>"},
{t:"Setup by application",h:"<ul>\n<li><b>PIM</b>: only change is \"Back-to-Back Enabled\" on the item in the shipping warehouse. Otherwise standard fulfilment runs.</li>\n<li><b>GOP</b>: ATP rule with Supply Chain Availability Search, all required supply types; tick \"Search components and resources\" for Make; infinite time fence beyond real lead times (30–40 day make → at least 41). Sourcing assignment type <b>Local</b>.</li>\n<li>GOP logic: stock in fulfilment org → On hand; upstream org → Transfer; can make in fulfilment org → Make; at supplier → Buy.</li>\n<li><b>OM/SCO</b>: no mandatory setup; predefined processes auto-assigned.</li>\n<li><b>Manufacturing</b> (Make): work definition for the item.</li>\n<li><b>Procurement</b> (Buy): feature Customer Sales Order Fulfillment; optional BPA with Automatically generate orders + auto-approval.</li>\n<li><b>Inventory</b>: no B2B-specific setup.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"focus\"><b>Exam focus</b>Item flag + GOP rules drive B2B; Inventory needs nothing specific.</div><div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: back-to-back part 1</b><ul>\n<li>Prerequisites in the exercise: <b>Back-to-Back Enabled</b> on the item in the fulfilment org, ATP and sourcing rules, and a <b>BPA</b> so requisitions become POs automatically.</li>\n<li>Order: customer, BU, bill-to account, item and quantity; Shipment Details → Supply tab → Warehouse 003 Chicago. Submit.</li>\n<li>Fulfillment View → Attributes → Supply Details → <b>Back-to-Back</b> section shows the supply order number. Its orchestration plan shows the requisition task complete; supply status <b>Awaiting supply</b>.</li></ul><small>Advanced Supply Chain & Fulfillment exercises</small></div>"},
{t:"Implementation considerations",h:"<ul>\n<li>Items should be MPS/MRP planned; use Purchased Item or Finished Good templates.</li>\n<li>Buy flow: default buyer and list price on the item.</li>\n<li>Run collections and refresh the Order Promising server often enough.</li>\n<li>Transit times with default ship methods for all location pairs.</li>\n<li>Transfer flow: item must be costed at least in the source org (transfer price derives from it).</li>\n<li>Specifying a supplier directly on the order turns the same item into a drop ship.</li></ul>"},
{t:"Change management and reservations",h:"<ul>\n<li>Date pushed out → exception + OM notified. Date pulled in → no change. Qty reduced → SCO splits and seeks alternate source.</li>\n<li>Partial shipment (23A+): supply line split to match, supply order stays open for the rest.</li>\n<li>Manual reservations when SCO can't create enough supply; demand changes to them are manual.</li>\n<li>Detailed reservation: after receipt, moves to on-hand at subinventory/locator/lot/serial (project/task for PDSC).</li></ul><div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: back-to-back part 2</b><ol>\n<li>Before receipt: Item Supply and Demand shows PO supply 10 and sales order reservation demand 10.</li>\n<li>Receive: Inventory Management → <b>Expected Shipment Lines</b> → Receive, subinventory Stores (direct delivery). Supply status becomes <b>Goods available</b>.</li>\n<li>Orchestration tasks: Purchase Requisition and Purchase Order = <b>DOS_BUY</b>, Reservation = <b>DOS_RESERVE</b>, Put Away = <b>DOS_RECEIVE</b>, Fulfillment Complete = <b>DOS_FULFILL</b>.</li>\n<li>Outbound Shipments → Ship Confirm → order <b>Awaiting Billing</b>, supply status <b>Supply order closed</b>.</li></ol><small>Advanced Supply Chain & Fulfillment exercises</small></div>"}
]});
MOD({id:"m5c",d:"d5",title:"Consigned inventory from supplier",
lede:"Supplier-owned stock at your site until you consume it, and how consumption is settled.",
topics:["Understand the consignment process","Set up consigned inventory","Manage consigned inventory transactions"],
sections:[
{t:"The flow",h:"<ol>\n<li>Consignment agreement → consignment order → receipt (same as normal).</li>\n<li>Consumption = ownership change supplier → buyer (or forced at end of aging period).</li>\n<li>Consumption advice to supplier (daily, weekly, monthly).</li>\n<li>Supplier invoice matched to the advice in Payables → payment. Optional pay on use (self-billing).</li></ol>\n<p>Benefits: buyer gets lower working capital and write-offs; supplier gets more sales and a stronger relationship.</p>\n<p class=\"src\">Source: Advanced Fulfillment, lessons 17–21</p>"},
{t:"Terms and setup",h:"<ul>\n<li>Consignment terms on the agreement (default from supplier site or procurement BU): aging onset point (<b>Receipt or Shipment</b>), aging period days, advice frequency (<b>Daily/Weekly/Monthly</b>), billing cycle closing date, advice summary, pay on use, default line as consignment.</li>\n<li>Consignment order: line flagged consignment; invoice match option = Consumption Advice.</li>\n<li>Setup tasks: Configure Procurement Business Function; Manage Supplier Sites; Manage Consumption Rules; Manage Cost Profiles (type Consigned).</li></ul>"},
{t:"Consumption",h:"<ul>\n<li><b>Explicit</b>: Create Transfer to Owned Transaction (e.g. near aging limit).</li>\n<li><b>Implicit</b>: a transaction type triggers it per consumption rules (SO issue, misc issue, transfers). Creates <b>two</b> transactions: ownership change + physical movement.</li>\n<li>Undo: Create Transfer to Consigned Transaction.</li>\n<li><b>Default rules</b>: inter-org movement = ownership change; intra-org movement = stays consigned. Rules by transaction type, from/to org, subinventory, locator, item, owning party.</li>\n<li>Consumption advice: scheduled process Create Consumption Advice; traceable to receipt, PO, agreement.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"focus\"><b>Exam focus</b>Default: inter-org = ownership change, intra-org = stays consigned. Implicit consumption = two transactions.</div>"},
{t:"Visibility, counting, returns and payables",h:"<ul>\n<li>Manage Item Quantities: \"Show consigned inventory only\", Consigned Details tab. Counts carry owning party.</li>\n<li>Returns any time; consigned and owned in one transaction.</li>\n<li>Supplier Inventory Manager role on the Supplier Portal: review advices, consigned stock and aging, Transfer to Owned/Consigned transactions.</li>\n<li>Pay on use must be enabled on <b>both</b> supplier site and agreement.</li>\n<li>Invoice tolerances: Consumed Percentage and Maximum Consumed Quantity (hold if billed > consumed).</li></ul>"}
]});
MOD({id:"m5d",d:"d5",title:"Project-driven supply chain (PDSC)",
lede:"Running inventory, procurement, manufacturing and maintenance in the context of a project, without separate orgs per project.",
topics:["Configure project-specific inventory management","Create project-specific inventory transactions"],
sections:[
{t:"The idea",h:"<ul>\n<li>Segregate stock by project and task in one warehouse; capture supply chain cost as project expenditures in PPM.</li>\n<li>Project and task become <b>inventory attributes</b> that segregate and value stock.</li>\n<li>Works even without Project Financials; Project Costing is needed for cost to flow to project accounting and GL.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"src\">Source: PDSC course, lessons 1–3; SCM Foundation, lesson 17</p>"},
{t:"Required setup (five)",h:"<ol>\n<li>Opt in: features <b>Project-Driven Supply Chain</b> and <b>Plan Project-Specific Supply</b>.</li>\n<li>Enable inventory tracking by project on each org (Manage Organization Parameters).</li>\n<li>Manage Default Expenditure Types: labour, material, non-labour, work order.</li>\n<li>Manage Project Organization Classifications: project and task owning org and project expenditure org.</li>\n<li>Orchestration process definition that skips Create Invoice for project lines (prjRecIndicator is null), since PPM bills.</li></ol>\n<p>Conditional: valuation structure → cost profile → valuation unit; project type cost exclusions (no expenditure sent to PPM).</p><div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: the common setups in practice</b><ol>\n<li><b>Opt in:</b> Setup and Maintenance → Manufacturing and Supply Chain Materials Management → <b>Change Feature Opt In</b> → Features (pencil) → Project-Driven Supply Chain + child Plan Project-Specific Supply.</li>\n<li><b>Tracking:</b> Manage Organization Parameters → General → Inventory Settings → <b>Enable inventory tracking by project</b> (next to the country-of-origin box), per org.</li>\n<li><b>Expenditure types:</b> Labor Resource = Supply Chain Labor; Material = Material; Nonlabor Resource = Supply Chain Resources; Work Order Header = Supply Chain Overhead. They must also be assigned to the project unit's reference data set (Manage Expenditure Types).</li>\n<li><b>Classification:</b> project and task owning org (Allow indirect projects = overhead projects; capitalisation; billing) and project expenditure org. Add to the tree <b>Project Organization Hierarchy</b> under the BU; the hierarchy must be the one named in Configure Project Accounting Business Function.</li>\n<li><b>Tree and process:</b> Manage Organization Trees → Flatten (row, online) and Set Status Active (online audit), then run <b>Maintain Project Organization</b>. Rerun it whenever orgs or hierarchies change, or when Expenditure Organization doesn't default.</li></ol>\n<p>Roles: setup by Supply Chain Application Administrator or Supply Chain Operations Manager; importing cost to projects needs <b>Project Accountant</b> with BU access.</p><small>PDSC activities</small></div>"},
{t:"Item attributes and common stock",h:"<ul>\n<li>Default Expenditure Type; Hard Pegging Level (None, Project, Project Group, Project and Task); Allow Use of Common Supplies.</li>\n<li>Pegging None + Allow common Null → common allowed. Pegging set + Allow common No → not allowed. Pegging set + Yes → allowed.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"focus\"><b>Exam focus</b>Common stock can feed project demand when pegging is None or Allow common = Yes.</div>"},
{t:"Project inventory transactions",h:"<ul>\n<li>Interorg transfer to a project via TO from requisition, SCO supply request or planning.</li>\n<li><b>Create Project Transfer</b> within an org: common ↔ project or project ↔ project.</li>\n<li>Misc issue from project stock via Manage Item Quantities.</li>\n<li>Transfer costing: from project stock = negative expenditure (from org) + positive (destination org).</li>\n<li>Procurement: approved requisition = commitment → moves to PO → relieved at receipt.</li>\n<li>Costing: Transfer Transactions from Inventory / Receiving / Production to Costing → distributions → Import Costs in Projects.</li>\n<li>Sales orders: project attributes changeable only until submit. WOs: editable while unreleased; expenditure item date = WO completion date.</li></ul><div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: project transactions and costing</b><ul>\n<li><b>Common in 001 → project in 002:</b> requisition line with <b>Source Type Inventory</b>, source org and subinventory; project, task, expenditure type and org under Billing Details → Project Costing. Approved → TO Awaiting Fulfillment → New Pick Wave (release rule 001-Auto Pick Conf, order type Transfer Order) → Ship Confirm → receive on Expected Shipment Lines (project fills in) → check the Item Quantities <b>Task</b> tab.</li>\n<li><b>Misc issue from project stock:</b> start on the project/task row so project and task prefill; set <b>Use Current Cost = Yes</b>.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"tbl\"><table><tr><th>Create Project Transfer</th><th>Fill in</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Common → project</td><td>Transfer-to project and task only</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Project → common</td><td>Transfer-from project and task only</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Project → project</td><td>Both</td></tr></table></div>\n<p><b>Costing chain:</b> Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing → Cost processing (run control, e.g. US_OPERATIONS) → Create Accounting (Cost Management, Inventory Transactions, Final, transfer and post to GL; report style Detail, No Report or Summary) → Projects → <b>Import Costs</b> (source Oracle Fusion Cost Management, status Not previously imported) → Manage Project Costs. Prerequisite: a journal entry rule set for event type <b>Project Transfer</b> in the accounting method.</p><small>PDSC activities</small></div>"}
]});
MOD({id:"m5e",d:"d5",title:"Other advanced topics",
lede:"Drop ship and contract manufacturing basics, plus exam topics not covered in your course material.",
topics:["Configure item replacement","Configure barcode scanning and label printing","Configure and execute product recall","Configure e-signatures and e-records"],
sections:[
{t:"Not covered in your course material",h:"<div class=\"gap\">The exam lists these topics, but none of your three books or the OM slides cover them. Look them up in the Oracle Inventory Management implementation and user guides or the quarterly What's New pages, then add them here:<ul>\n<li>Configure item replacement for inventory entities</li>\n<li>Configure barcode scanning and label printing for mobile inventory</li>\n<li>Configure and execute product recall</li></ul>\nNo quiz questions are included for these yet, so nothing unverified gets into your practice exams.</div>\n<p>E-signatures and e-records are covered under Transaction setup & material status.</p>"},
{t:"Drop ship essentials",h:"<ul>\n<li>Supplier ships straight to your customer; you hold no stock. Chosen when GOP schedules to a supplier (or a supplier is on the order).</li>\n<li>Features: OM \"Drop Ship\" + Procurement \"Customer Sales Order Fulfillment\". Sourcing rule type <b>Global</b> Buy From.</li>\n<li>Drop ship financial flow sets the receiving trade organisation (logical receiving org). Ownership event: ASN or supplier invoice.</li>\n<li>Preparer for Procurement in OM parameters is mandatory.</li>\n<li>Line statuses: Scheduled → Requisition Created → Awaiting Shipping → Shipped → Awaiting Billing → Billed.</li>\n<li>Requisition stage: cancellation only. Drop ship PO quantity can't be increased.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: drop ship and a change</b><ul>\n<li>BPA → Controls → Order Creation Options: <b>Automatically generate orders</b> and <b>Automatically submit for approval</b> (plus group requisitions, use customer sales order). Business Unit Access sets the requisitioning BU.</li>\n<li>Line statuses seen: Scheduled → Requisition Created → Awaiting Shipping. Drop ship PO: Fulfillment View → Attributes → Supply Details → <b>Drop Shipment</b> section.</li>\n<li>Supplier Portal → Advance Shipment Notices → Purchase Orders to Ship → <b>Create ASN</b>. The ASN is the shipment confirmation; the order goes to Awaiting Billing.</li>\n<li>Change: Actions → <b>Create Revision</b> (shows \"(2) – Draft\") → quantity 3 → 5 → Submit; the drop ship PO follows. This only worked because the processing constraint <b>DOO_DS_FULFILLMENT_LINE_UPDATE</b> was disabled for training; normally it blocks changes the supplier may no longer accept.</li></ul><small>Advanced Supply Chain & Fulfillment exercises</small></div>\n<p class=\"src\">Source: Advanced Fulfillment, lessons 9–12</p>"},
{t:"Contract manufacturing essentials",h:"<ul>\n<li>OEM outsources; SCO pairs a WO (tracks progress) with a PO for a service item (the contract).</li>\n<li>CM = supplier + site AND an external inventory org with \"manufacturing plant\" and \"represents a contract manufacturer\" = Yes.</li>\n<li>Service item: Buy, Contract Manufacturing = Yes. FG item: Make, Contract Manufacturing = Yes; structure includes the service item.</li>\n<li>Service item on the last count-point operation as operation pull; work definition attached to the BPA \"To Supplier\".</li>\n<li>Plan-to-produce: no reservation, no OM exception. Back-to-back: WO reserved to SO, exceptions on the SO.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"lab\"><b>Hands-on: the CM organisation</b><ul>\n<li>Manage Inventory Organizations → Boise: <b>External</b>, linked to the CM supplier and site.</li>\n<li>Parameters → General → Additional Usages: \"Organization is a manufacturing plant\" is ticked and <b>greyed out</b>, because it's required for a CM org; \"performs maintenance activities\" is unticked.</li></ul><small>Advanced Supply Chain & Fulfillment exercises</small></div>\n<p class=\"src\">Source: Advanced Fulfillment, lessons 22–27</p>"}
]});
QS("m5a",[
["What is the default execution document SCO creates for a transfer request?",["Transfer order","Purchase order","Sales order","Work order"],"Default is TO; a creation rule can switch to PO."],
["By default, where does SCO send a transfer order?",["Directly to Inventory","Through Order Management","To Procurement","To Planning"],"Defaulting and enrichment rules default to Inventory; OM routing is optional."],
["Which scheduled process picks up supply requests from the interface?",["Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface","Requisition Import","Create Supply Request","Transfer Transactions to Costing"],"Interface data is processed by Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface."],
["A supply line failed because a reservation couldn't be created. Which bucket?",["Errors","Exceptions","Jeopardy","On-track"],"Errors are technical or functional failures that stop a transaction."],
["Supply no longer matches demand and automatic change management couldn't fix it. Which bucket?",["Exceptions","Errors","Jeopardy","On-track"],"Exceptions = mismatch not resolved by change management."],
["A PO is promised after the sales order need-by date. Which bucket?",["Jeopardy","Exceptions","Errors","On-track"],"Jeopardy = supply late vs need-by date."],
["What's the difference between supply and order orchestration?",["Supply orchestration may not relate to a sales order; order orchestration always does","They're the same","Order orchestration creates POs","Supply orchestration ships to customers"],"Supply gets goods into your warehouse; order gets them to the customer."],
["Demand is 100; the supplier cuts the PO to 75. What does SCO do first?",["Look for an alternate source for 25","Cancel the sales order","Raise an error","Increase the PO"],"It locks the line and seeks another source; if none, it raises an exception."],
["Which rule decides whether a TO is routed through OM?",["Supply order defaulting and enrichment rules","Execution document creation rules","Sourcing rules","ATP rules"],"Enrichment rules control OM routing."],
["What is the suggested key for execution document creation rules?",["Source org and destination org","Customer and item","Supplier and buyer","Carrier and route"],"Suggested: source + destination org, or item + both orgs."],
["Which tool renders rules for execution document and enrichment?",["Oracle Business Rules UI","Workflow approvals","Groovy only","FBDI"],"Both open the OBR (business rules) UI."],
["Which role sees all supply orders by default?",["Supply Chain Operations Manager","Warehouse Manager","Buyer","Order Manager"],"The predefined Supply Chain Operations Manager has full access."],
["After changing SCO data security, which process must you run?",["Import User and Role Application Security Data","Refresh Order Promising Server","Process SCO Interface","Collect Planning Data"],"Security changes need Import User and Role Application Security Data."],
["What does the service mapper let you do?",["Pass extra attributes such as sales order EFFs to downstream documents","Map GL accounts","Map suppliers to orgs","Map UOMs"],"It enriches downstream requests with custom mappings."],
["Which supply types appear on the Supply Lines Overview?",["Make, Buy, Transfer, ATP","Stock, Expense, Asset","PO, SO, RMA","Direct, In-transit, Consigned"],"Supply type: Make, Buy, Transfer and ATP (reserved on-hand/expected)."],
["Which scheduled process picks up supply requests from a source system into Supply Chain Orchestration?",["Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface","Print Min-Max Planning Report","Create Inventory Replenishment Request Process","Requisition Import"],"Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface processes the SCO interface data."],
["You want only the supply requests raised from Item Quantities or transfer requests to be processed. Which Supply Request System do you choose?",["Oracle Fusion Inventory Management","Oracle Fusion Order Management","External","Oracle Fusion Planning Central"],"Requests from Item Quantities come from the Inventory Management source system."],
["Which two tiles appear on the Supply Chain Orchestration Overview page?",["Supply Requests and Supply Alerts","Errors and Exceptions","Supply Lines and Supply Orders","Jeopardy and On-track"],"The overview shows Supply Requests and Supply Alerts."],
["Where do you see the components of a supply such as receipt, reservation, PO and requisition?",["Supply Request Line Details → Supply Details section","The supply request header","Order Management → Order Lines","Manage Interorganization Parameters"],"Supply Details on the line lists the underlying documents."],
["What does the Service Mapping Details section on a supply request line show?",["Entities and attributes mapped downstream, e.g. note to supplier on the purchase request line","The orchestration tasks and their status","The ranked list of source orgs","Errors and exceptions for the line"],"Service mappings carry demand attributes into the execution documents."],
["In SCO, which part of the supply request holds the orchestration plan and execution documents?",["The supply line","The supply request header","The service mapping","The Supply Alerts tile"],"The header is the request; the line holds the plan and documents."]
]);
QS("m5b",[
["What is the only PIM setup needed for back-to-back?",["Back-to-Back Enabled on the item in the shipping warehouse","A back-to-back item template","Lot control","A B2B catalog"],"The item flag per org is the only product setup."],
["A line is scheduled to an internal warehouse and the item isn't B2B enabled. Which process runs?",["Standard","Back-to-back","Drop ship","Transfer"],"Internal warehouse + not B2B enabled → standard fulfilment."],
["A line is scheduled to a supplier. Which process runs?",["Drop ship","Back-to-back buy","Standard","Contract manufacturing"],"Scheduled to supplier → drop ship."],
["Which ATP promising mode supports back-to-back?",["Supply chain availability search","Infinite availability","ATP only","Lead-time based"],"Use Supply Chain Availability Search with the required supply types."],
["For back-to-back, the ATP rule's infinite availability time fence must lie beyond the longest real lead time, otherwise GOP assumes unlimited supply too early. Making the item takes 30 to 40 days. What is the minimum time fence?",["41 days","30 days","35 days","0 days"],"The fence must be past the longest lead time (40 days), so at least 41 days."],
["What sourcing rule assignment type is used for back-to-back?",["Local","Global","Supplier","Drop ship"],"B2B sourcing uses Organization Assignment Type = Local."],
["Stock exists in an upstream org defined in the local sourcing rule. What does GOP recommend?",["Transfer","On hand","Make","Buy"],"Upstream org → Transfer recommendation."],
["What must exist for a back-to-back Make recommendation?",["A work definition for the item","A BPA","A transfer pricing rule","A consignment agreement"],"GOP needs a collected work definition to recommend Make."],
["Which Procurement feature is needed for back-to-back Buy?",["Customer Sales Order Fulfillment","Drop Ship","Internal Material Transfer","Consignment"],"Enable Customer Sales Order Fulfillment."],
["What Inventory setup is specific to back-to-back?",["None","A B2B subinventory","A B2B material status","A B2B transaction type"],"Inventory needs no B2B-specific setup."],
["A supplier pushes a B2B PO promise date out. What happens?",["Exception on the SCO workbench and OM is notified","Nothing","The SO is cancelled","A new PO is created automatically"],"Date push-out → exception + OM notified."],
["A supplier pulls a B2B PO date in. What happens?",["No change to supply or sales order","The SO ship date moves earlier","An exception is raised","The reservation is removed"],"Date pull-in causes no change."],
["For B2B transfer, what must be true about item cost?",["The item must be costed at least in the source org","Cost is optional","The item must have standard cost","Cost is only needed at destination"],"Transfer price derives from source org cost."],
["When do you create manual reservations in a B2B flow?",["When SCO can't create enough supply","Always","Only for serial items","Never"],"Manual reservations cover shortfalls; demand changes then need manual handling."],
["Which are the four back-to-back variants?",["Buy, Make, Transfer, On hand","Buy, Make, Drop ship, Consign","PO, SO, WO, RMA","Standard, Express, Direct, Split"],"GOP recommends one of Buy, Make, Transfer or On hand."],
["Which of these is NOT a prerequisite for back-to-back fulfilment?",["Interorganization parameters between the warehouse and the customer","Back-to-Back Enabled on the item in the fulfilment org","ATP rules and sourcing rules","A BPA so requisitions become POs automatically"],"Interorg parameters are for org-to-org transfers. The customer isn't an inventory org."],
["Where is Back-to-Back Enabled set?",["On the item (Product Information Management), in the fulfilment organisation","On the customer account","In Order Management parameters","On the BPA"],"It's an item attribute in the fulfilment org."],
["Put the back-to-back supply status values in order.",["Awaiting supply → Goods available → Supply order closed","Goods available → Awaiting supply → Supply order closed","Awaiting supply → Supply order closed → Goods available","Requisition Created → Awaiting Shipping → Shipped"],"Supply arrives (goods available) and closes when the order ships."],
["In the back-to-back orchestration plan, which task type matches Put Away?",["DOS_RECEIVE","DOS_BUY","DOS_RESERVE","DOS_FULFILL"],"DOS_BUY = requisition and PO; DOS_RESERVE = reservation; DOS_RECEIVE = put away; DOS_FULFILL = completion."],
["A back-to-back sales order for 10 units has created a purchase order for 10. Before the PO is received, what does Review Item Supply and Demand show in the warehouse?",["PO supply of 10 matched by sales order reservation demand of 10","On hand of 10 with no demand","Sales order demand of 10 with no supply","Transfer order supply of 10"],"The PO is the supply, and the sales order is reserved against it until receipt."],
["Which Inventory Management action do you use to receive the back-to-back PO?",["Inbound Shipments → Expected Shipment Lines → Receive","Outbound Shipments → Ship Confirm","SCO → Manage Supply Lines → Resubmit","Supplier Portal → Create ASN"],"Back-to-back POs are received like any other expected shipment."],
["After Ship Confirm on the back-to-back order, what is the sales order status?",["Awaiting Billing","Closed","Shipped","Awaiting Shipping"],"Shipping moves the order to Awaiting Billing."],
["Which three things make a back-to-back order create a supply order that turns into a PO automatically?",["Back-to-Back Enabled on the item in the fulfilment org, ATP/sourcing rules, and a BPA","Interorg parameters, a transfer order type and a pick wave","A drop ship sourcing rule, an ASN and a receiving org","A consigned agreement, an aging period and a consumption rule"],"The item flag triggers back-to-back, GOP rules pick the supply, and the BPA lets the requisition become a PO without a buyer."]
]);
QS("m5c",[
["What are the aging onset point options?",["Receipt or Shipment","Order or Receipt","Invoice or Payment","Consumption or Advice"],"Aging starts at receipt or shipment."],
["Which consumption advice frequencies exist?",["Daily, Weekly, Monthly","Hourly, Daily","Per transaction only","Quarterly, Yearly"],"Advice frequency: daily, weekly or monthly."],
["By default, what does moving consigned stock between two subinventories in the same org do?",["It stays consigned","It changes ownership","It's blocked","It creates a consumption advice immediately"],"Default rule: intra-org movement stays consigned."],
["By default, what does moving consigned stock to another inventory org do?",["It changes ownership to the buyer","It stays consigned","It creates a return","It resets aging"],"Default rule: inter-org movement = ownership change."],
["How many transactions does an implicit consumption create?",["Two: ownership change and physical movement","One","Three","None until advice runs"],"Implicit consumption creates the ownership change plus the movement."],
["Which transaction explicitly takes ownership of consigned stock?",["Create Transfer to Owned Transaction","Create Transfer to Consigned Transaction","Miscellaneous receipt","Consumption advice"],"Transfer to Owned is the explicit consumption."],
["A consumption was recorded by mistake. How do you reverse it?",["Create Transfer to Consigned Transaction","Delete the consumption advice","Run a misc receipt","Cancel the PO"],"Transfer to Consigned finds the original transaction and reverses it."],
["What is the invoice match option on a consignment order line?",["Consumption Advice","Receipt","Order","None"],"Invoices match to consumption advices, not the order."],
["Pay on use must be enabled where?",["On both the supplier site and the agreement","Only the supplier site","Only the agreement","On the inventory org"],"Both site and agreement."],
["Which invoice tolerances apply to consignment?",["Consumed Percentage and Maximum Consumed Quantity","Price and quantity received","Amount and date","Over-receipt and early receipt"],"They place holds if billed quantity exceeds consumed."],
["Which scheduled process creates consumption advices?",["Create Consumption Advice","Transfer to Owned","Process SCO Interface","Send Pay on Receipt"],"Create Consumption Advice builds advices per frequency."],
["Which supplier-side role reviews consigned stock and aging?",["Supplier Inventory Manager","Supplier Customer Service","Warehouse Manager","Buyer"],"Supplier Inventory Manager on the Supplier Portal."],
["How do you view only consigned stock in Manage Item Quantities?",["'Show consigned inventory only'","Filter by material status","Filter by lot grade","Use the Inbound tab"],"Use that option; the Consigned Details tab shows owning party."],
["Which cost profile type is needed for consigned items?",["Consigned","Standard","Actual","Expense"],"Manage Cost Profiles with type Consigned, via item or default profiles."],
["Can consigned and owned quantities be returned in one transaction?",["Yes","No","Only after consumption","Only for lot items"],"Returns can mix consigned and owned stock."]
]);
QS("m5d",[
["What is the core benefit of PDSC?",["Segregating stock by project without separate inventory orgs","A separate org per project","Automatic project billing in Receivables","Replacing Project Costing"],"PDSC stripes stock by project/task in the same org."],
["Which two features do you opt into for PDSC?",["Project-Driven Supply Chain and Plan Project-Specific Supply","Project Costing and Project Billing","Consignment and PDSC","Drop Ship and PDSC"],"Both features under Manufacturing and SC Materials Mgmt."],
["Where do you enable inventory tracking by project?",["Organization parameters of each inventory org","Item attributes","Subinventory definition","Receiving parameters"],"Tick 'Enable inventory tracking by project' per org."],
["Why change the orchestration process definition for project lines?",["To skip invoicing in Receivables because PPM bills","To add a project approval step","To route to Procurement","To reserve stock"],"The Create Invoice step runs only when the project record indicator is null."],
["Hard pegging = Project and Allow Use of Common Supplies = No. Can common stock satisfy project demand?",["No","Yes","Only with approval","Only for transfer orders"],"Pegging set + Allow common No → common not allowed."],
["Hard pegging = None. What is Allow Use of Common Supplies and can common be used?",["Null, and common is allowed","Yes, and common is blocked","No, and common is blocked","It's mandatory Yes"],"Pegging None → Allow common Null → common allowed."],
["Which transaction moves stock from common to project within one org?",["Create Project Transfer","Subinventory transfer","Misc receipt","Transfer order"],"Create Project Transfer handles common ↔ project and project ↔ project."],
["How is a transfer from project stock costed?",["Negative expenditure for the from-org and positive for the destination org","A single positive expenditure","No expenditure","Only a GL entry"],"From project stock: negative + positive expenditures."],
["When is a project commitment created in PPM?",["When the requisition is approved","When the PO is received","When the invoice is paid","When the WO completes"],"Approved requisition → commitment → moves to PO → relieved at receipt."],
["Which process sends receipt costs to Costing for project POs?",["Transfer Transactions from Receiving to Costing","Import Costs","Create Accounting","Process SCO Interface"],"Receiving → Costing, then distributions and Import Costs."],
["When can project attributes on a sales order line be changed?",["Only until the order is submitted","Until ship confirm","Any time","Never"],"Project attributes change only until submit."],
["What is the default expenditure item date on a project work order?",["The WO completion date","The WO release date","Today","The requested ship date"],"Defaults: date = WO completion date; org = plant."],
["What does a project type cost exclusion do?",["Stops expenditure being sent to PPM for that project type","Blocks all transactions","Excludes items from planning","Removes project from reports"],"Excluded types: no expenditure interfaced, no commitment, COGS stays in Cost Management."],
["Which classification must each project inventory org have?",["Project and task owning org and project expenditure org","Cost organisation","Item master","Legal entity"],"Set in Manage Project Organization Classifications."],
["Which is a conditional costing setup for PDSC?",["Valuation structure with project and task, then cost profile and valuation unit","Accrue at receipt","A new cost book per project","Landed cost charges"],"Valuation by project needs structure → profile → unit."],
["Which two features must be enabled in the Manufacturing and Supply Chain Materials Management opt-in for PDSC?",["Project-Driven Supply Chain and Plan Project-Specific Supply","Project Costing and Project Billing","Hard Pegging and Common Supplies","Customer Sales Order Fulfillment and Drop Ship"],"Plan Project-Specific Supply is a child of Project-Driven Supply Chain."],
["Where do you opt in to PDSC?",["Setup and Maintenance → Manufacturing and Supply Chain Materials Management → Change Feature Opt In → Features","Manage Administrator Profile Values","Project Financial Management → Manage Project Types","Manage Inventory Organizations"],"It's an offering-level feature."],
["Which role, with access to the BU, is needed to import cost to projects?",["Project Accountant","Warehouse Manager","Cost Accountant","Buyer"],"Project Accountant (ORA_PJF_PROJECT_ACCOUNTANT_JOB)."],
["Where is 'Enable inventory tracking by project' set?",["Manage Inventory Organizations → Manage Organization Parameters → General tab","Item attributes","Manage Default Expenditure Types","Project Unit setup"],"It's an org parameter under Inventory Settings."],
["On Manage Default Expenditure Types, which four categories do you set a default expenditure type for?",["Labor resource, Material, Nonlabor resource, Work order header","Material, Freight, Tax, Overhead","Receipt, Issue, Transfer, Adjustment","Buy, Make, Transfer, Consign"],"Supply chain transactions costed to a project use these four defaults (in the course data: Supply Chain Labor, Material, Supply Chain Resources, Supply Chain Overhead)."],
["Which default expenditure type category is used for overhead charged at work order level?",["Work order header","Material","Labor resource","Nonlabor resource"],"Work order header covers overhead; in the course data it maps to Supply Chain Overhead."],
["What extra condition must default expenditure types meet to be usable on a project?",["They must be assigned to the reference data set of the project's project unit","They must have the same name as the project","They must be linked to an ABC class","They must be created by the Project Accountant"],"Done in Manage Expenditure Types (e.g. Consulting Services Set)."],
["Which classification does an inventory org need to receive project expenditures?",["Project expenditure organization","Profit centre business unit","Item organisation","Cost organisation"],"In the practice it's also classified as project and task owning org."],
["Which org hierarchy must the project expenditure orgs belong to?",["The one specified in Configure Project Accounting Business Function for the BU","Any HCM hierarchy","The inventory org tree","The cost organisation hierarchy"],"Here: Project Organization Hierarchy."],
["After adding orgs to the tree version, which two tree actions come before the process run?",["Flatten (row, online) and Set Status → Active (online audit)","Publish and Approve","Copy and Rename","Export and Import"],"Then run Maintain Project Organization."],
["Which scheduled process maintains org info in Project Financial Management after classification or hierarchy changes?",["Maintain Project Organization","Process Supply Chain Orchestration Interface","Create Accounting","Refresh Organization Tree Cache"],"It also fixes a missing Expenditure Organization."],
["What does 'Allow indirect projects' on a project-owning org allow?",["The org can own projects that collect and track overhead costs","The org can bill customers directly","The org can capitalise assets","The org can skip costing"],"Indirect projects are for overhead."],
["In the project-specific interorg transfer, which Source Type is chosen on the requisition line?",["Inventory","Supplier","Transfer Order","Project"],"Source Type Inventory makes it an internal transfer."],
["Where are project and task entered on the requisition?",["Billing Details → Project Costing","Line header → Item","Delivery → Subinventory","Approval → Rule set"],"Project Number, Task, Expenditure Type and Expenditure Organization sit there."],
["Put these in order: ship confirm, requisition approved, receive in destination, release pick wave, transfer order created.",["Requisition approved → TO created → pick wave → ship confirm → receive","TO created → requisition approved → ship confirm → pick wave → receive","Pick wave → requisition approved → TO created → receive → ship confirm","Requisition approved → pick wave → TO created → receive → ship confirm"],"The requisition drives SCO to create the TO, which is then picked, shipped and received."],
["A pick wave for a project transfer order should be pick-confirmed automatically, without a separate confirmation step. Where is that behaviour set?",["In the release rule used to release the pick wave","In the interorganization parameters","On the transfer order line","In the project's billing details"],"Auto pick confirm is a release rule setting (the course uses a rule called 001-Auto Pick Conf)."],
["On Item Quantities, where do you check that received stock carries project and task?",["The Task tab (or Project tab)","The Subinventory tab","The Lot tab","The Inbound tab"],"Project stock is visible by project and task."],
["On Create Project Transfer, which fields do you fill for common → project?",["Only Transfer-to Project and Transfer-to Task","Only Transfer-from Project and Task","Both from and to","None; the system infers it"],"No source project for common stock."],
["On Create Project Transfer, which fields do you fill for project → common?",["Only Transfer-from Project and Transfer-from Task","Only Transfer-to Project and Task","Both from and to","Source subinventory only"],"Leave the to-fields empty to return to common."],
["On Create Project Transfer, which fields do you fill for project → project?",["Both Transfer-from and Transfer-to Project and Task","Only Transfer-to fields","Only Transfer-from fields","Project only, without task"],"All three variations use the same page; the fields decide the type."],
["Which More Actions option on Item Quantities starts a project transfer?",["Create Project Transfer","Create Interorganization Transfer","Create Movement Request Transfer","Change Material Status"],"Create Project Transfer handles all three variants."],
["For a project miscellaneous issue, which option controls the cost used?",["Use Current Cost = Yes","Cost Book = Financial","Report Style = Summary","Account Alias"],"Use Current Cost is set on the transaction line."],
["Which scheduled process moves inventory transactions into Cost Management?",["Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing","Create Accounting","Import Costs","Maintain Project Organization"],"It's the first step in the costing chain."],
["Which Cost Accounting page runs cost processing for a cost org and cost book?",["Cost processing run control","Review Journal Entries","Item Costs","Costing Transactions and Distributions"],"E.g. run control US_OPERATIONS."],
["For Create Accounting on inventory costing, which Subledger Application and Process Category do you use?",["Cost Management; Inventory Transactions","Receipt Accounting; Receipts","Projects; Costs","General Ledger; Journals"],"Cost Management subledger, Inventory Transactions category."],
["Which Report Style options does Create Accounting offer?",["Detail, No Report, Summary","Full, Partial, None","PDF, Excel, HTML","Draft, Final, Preview"],"Detail, No Report and Summary."],
["Which accounting setup lets project transfers be accounted?",["A journal entry rule set for event type Project Transfer in the accounting method","A new cost book","A project type with cost exclusions","An interorg transfer price"],"E.g. US Standard Accrual, Cost Management scope, event class Interorganization Transfer."],
["In Import Costs, which Transaction Source brings inventory costs into Projects?",["Oracle Fusion Cost Management","Oracle Fusion Inventory Management","Oracle Fusion Payables","External"],"Costs come from Cost Management."],
["In Import Costs, which Transaction Status value picks up only new transactions?",["Not previously imported","Imported with errors","All","Rejected"],"Use Not previously imported for new ones."],
["Where do you review the imported project cost?",["Projects → Costs → Manage Project Costs → Project Cost Transaction","Inventory → Completed Transactions","Cost Accounting → Item Costs","General Ledger → Journals"],"General and Costing tabs show expenditure details and raw/burdened cost."],
["What is the right order of the PDSC costing chain?",["Transfer to Costing → Cost processing → Create Accounting → Import Costs","Create Accounting → Transfer to Costing → Import Costs → Cost processing","Import Costs → Cost processing → Create Accounting → Transfer to Costing","Cost processing → Transfer to Costing → Import Costs → Create Accounting"],"Transactions must be costed and accounted before import to projects."],
["What should you check if Expenditure Organization doesn't default on a project requisition?",["Run Maintain Project Organization","Re-opt in to PDSC","Recreate the item","Run Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing"],"Maintain Project Organization fixes missing org information in Project Financial Management."],
["When receiving a project transfer order, how do project and task get onto the receipt?",["They populate automatically from the requisition and TO","You re-enter them on every receipt","They come from the subinventory","They're added later by Import Costs"],"Project and task on the requisition distribution carry through the TO, shipment and receipt."]
]);
QS("m5e",[
["Which sourcing rule type is used for drop ship?",["Global Buy From","Local Transfer From","Local Make At","Global Transfer From"],"Drop ship uses a Global Buy From rule."],
["What happens to a drop ship purchase request if Preparer for Procurement isn't set?",["Procurement rejects it","It defaults to the buyer","It creates an unapproved PO","It goes to SCO"],"Preparer for Procurement is mandatory."],
["What triggers the ownership change in a drop ship financial flow?",["ASN or supplier invoice","Sales order booking","Requisition approval","Customer receipt"],"You choose ASN or AP invoice as the ownership event."],
["What is the correct drop ship line status order?",["Scheduled, Requisition Created, Awaiting Shipping, Shipped, Awaiting Billing, Billed","Scheduled, Shipped, Billed","Requisition Created, Scheduled, Shipped","Booked, Picked, Shipped, Billed"],"This is the fulfilment line sequence."],
["At requisition stage (no PO yet), which drop ship change is allowed?",["Cancellation only","Quantity increase","Date change","Supplier change"],"Procurement accepts only cancellation at that stage."],
["Which change can a buyer NOT make on a drop ship PO?",["Increase quantity","Change promise date","Split schedule","Cancel schedule"],"Quantity increases aren't allowed on drop ship POs."],
["In contract manufacturing, what is the service item?",["A Buy item on the PO representing the CM's work","The finished good","A component supplied by the OEM","A phantom item"],"Service item = Buy, CM = Yes, on the PO."],
["Which org flags are set for a CM inventory organisation?",["Manufacturing plant = Yes and represents a contract manufacturer = Yes","Item org = Yes","Consigned = Yes","Project enabled = Yes"],"Both flags, and link supplier + site."],
["Where is the service item placed in the CM work definition?",["On the last count-point operation as an operation-pull component","On the first operation","It isn't in the work definition","On a phantom operation"],"So FG cost = service + supplied components."],
["What differs in plan-to-produce CM vs back-to-back CM?",["Plan-to-produce has no reservation and no OM exception","Plan-to-produce reserves to a sales order","Back-to-back has no PO","They're identical"],"P2P: no reservation; if a change can't be met, no response."],
["Which BPA Order Creation Options let a drop ship requisition turn into a PO automatically?",["Automatically generate orders and Automatically submit for approval","Group requisitions and Use customer sales order only","Pay on use and consumption advice frequency","Allow price override and enforce ship-to"],"Those two options create and submit the PO without a buyer."],
["After submitting a drop ship order, in what order does the fulfilment line status change?",["Scheduled → Requisition Created → Awaiting Shipping","Requisition Created → Scheduled → Awaiting Shipping","Scheduled → Awaiting Shipping → Requisition Created","Awaiting supply → Goods available → Supply order closed"],"Requisition first, then the PO leaves the line awaiting the supplier's shipment."],
["Where is the drop ship PO number found on the sales order?",["Fulfillment View → Attributes → Supply Details → Drop Shipment section","Order header → General tab","Purchase Agreements page","SCO Overview"],"The Drop Shipment section holds supplier, PO and requisition details."],
["In the drop ship flow, what does the supplier do that counts as shipment confirmation?",["Creates an ASN in the Supplier Portal","Receives the PO","Runs Ship Confirm in Inventory","Creates an invoice"],"The supplier's ASN confirms the shipment."],
["Where does the supplier create the ASN?",["Supplier Portal → Advance Shipment Notices → Purchase Orders to Ship → Create ASN","Order Management → Manage Orders","Inventory Management → Outbound Shipments","Procurement → Purchase Agreements"],"ASNs are created from the supplier's portal."],
["Which processing constraint was disabled so a drop ship order change could flow to the PO?",["DOO_DS_FULFILLMENT_LINE_UPDATE","DOO_DS_FULFILLMENT_LINE_CANCEL","ORDER DELETION","ORDER LINE DELETION"],"It sits under Setup and Maintenance → Order Management → Orders → Manage Processing Constraints."],
["Why does the DOO_DS_FULFILLMENT_LINE_UPDATE constraint exist?",["To block order changes that would revise the drop ship PO once the supplier probably can't accept them","To stop drop ship orders being cancelled at requisition stage","To prevent duplicate ASNs","To force a new order instead of a revision"],"It protects the supplier relationship from late changes."],
["After Create Revision on a sales order, how is it shown before submission?",["As version 2 in Draft, e.g. \"(2) – Draft\"","As version 1 Open","As version 2 Processing","As a new order number"],"A revision creates a new draft version until submitted."],
["How is a contract manufacturer modelled in the OEM's Fusion instance?",["As an external inventory org that is a manufacturing plant, linked to the CM supplier and site","As an internal inventory org only","As a customer account","As a subinventory of the OEM plant"],"The CM is both supplier/site and an external manufacturing-plant org."],
["Why is 'Organization is a manufacturing plant' greyed out for the contract manufacturing org?",["For a manufacturing plant those usages are required and can't be edited","The org is inactive","The user lacks the privilege","It's set by a profile option"],"Required usages are locked for a manufacturing plant."],
["By default, why couldn't you simply raise a drop ship order quantity after the PO went to the supplier?",["The processing constraint DOO_DS_FULFILLMENT_LINE_UPDATE blocks it","Drop ship orders can't be revised at all","The BPA is closed","The ASN has already been created"],"The constraint protects against changes the supplier may no longer accept; it was disabled only for training."]
]);
